# Case: Real guest close, background capture and second launch
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Verify that closing the native main window preserves tray capture and second launch creates a new GUI process.
# Steps:
#   Close the focused owned main window through physical Alt+F4, offer fresh text while the GUI process is absent, launch the same application identity again, then reopen history and quit at cleanup.
# Expected:
#   The tray retains its service and captures exact fresh content after the GUI exits; second launch exits and preserves the service generation; the new GUI process becomes visible; explicit Quit reaps the owner and service.
# Forbidden:
#   Closing unrelated applications, replacing the active service, or treating a process fixture as a native close.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D lifecycle startup baseline'
start
system-key Alt+F4
# Main-window close now means that the GUI process has exited.
system-window unic hidden
system-board-write 'UNIC-D capture while GUI absent 中文'
history-count 1
system-second-launch
system-window unic visible
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D capture while GUI absent 中文'
screenshot recreated-gui
